WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.633 --> 00:00:05.009
- Today we're gonna be matching
some weird Amazon products

00:00:05.009 --> 00:00:07.667
to some equally weird Amazon reviews,

00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:11.667
and we're gonna see if
we get them right or not.

00:00:32.103 --> 00:00:34.718
- [Narrator] "If I could give
this a million stars I would.

00:00:34.718 --> 00:00:37.941
"I love it so much I couldn't
even bring myself to use it.

00:00:37.941 --> 00:00:39.261
"I drew a face on it.

00:00:39.261 --> 00:00:42.074
"Now it's my friend and I
have a little over 40 of them!

00:00:42.074 --> 00:00:43.504
"I am soon ordering more.

00:00:43.504 --> 00:00:44.418
"I LOVE THESE!

00:00:44.418 --> 00:00:46.697
"They are a gift from god!"

00:00:46.697 --> 00:00:48.031
- Look at this!

00:00:48.031 --> 00:00:48.864
- It's not.

00:00:48.864 --> 00:00:50.793
No it's definitely crafting with cat hair.

00:00:50.793 --> 00:00:53.799
- You can't draw a face on a
vacuum or a book I feel like,

00:00:53.799 --> 00:00:54.842
or a head game.

00:00:54.842 --> 00:00:57.337
- Yeah so lets just go, eliminate.

00:00:57.337 --> 00:00:58.797
- I hope it's not that pickle.

00:00:58.797 --> 00:01:00.337
- You can draw a face on a sponge,

00:01:00.337 --> 00:01:02.226
and if you are a good budgeter,

00:01:02.226 --> 00:01:05.170
you can get 40 sponges
for quite a good price.

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:07.051
- I would draw a face on these,

00:01:07.051 --> 00:01:09.384
because it's like SpongeBob.

00:01:10.315 --> 00:01:11.179
- [Narrator] "We purchased this

00:01:11.179 --> 00:01:13.251
"and gave it to 'Weird
Al Yankovic' as a gift.

00:01:13.251 --> 00:01:14.864
"He liked it so much he posted it

00:01:14.864 --> 00:01:16.039
"to his Twitter and Instagram.

00:01:16.039 --> 00:01:17.584
"If the weirdest guy
on the planet approves,

00:01:17.584 --> 00:01:18.885
"How can you go wrong?

00:01:18.885 --> 00:01:20.228
"Highly recommended."

00:01:20.228 --> 00:01:22.433
- Or could it be the head game?

00:01:22.433 --> 00:01:23.860
- I loved Weird Al growing up.

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:25.167
- Oh I didn't.

00:01:25.167 --> 00:01:26.962
(pickle yodels)

00:01:26.962 --> 00:01:29.006
- Oh that's gotta be it.

00:01:29.006 --> 00:01:29.852
- He's weird.

00:01:29.852 --> 00:01:34.019
- It's either this yodeling
pickle, or the head game.

00:01:35.469 --> 00:01:36.302
- [Narrator] Review number 3,

00:01:36.302 --> 00:01:37.925
"This was probably the
most awesome Christmas gift

00:01:37.925 --> 00:01:39.954
"I could have ever give my four year old."

00:01:39.954 --> 00:01:42.434
- I was gonna go for the head games.

00:01:42.434 --> 00:01:44.646
- I just think ya know,
that's too obvious.

00:01:44.646 --> 00:01:47.281
- I could see a four year old
just livin' life right now.

00:01:47.281 --> 00:01:49.599
I'm 25 and I'll live life with this thing.

00:01:49.599 --> 00:01:52.027
- Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

00:01:52.027 --> 00:01:54.672
Context clue, this is for six and up.

00:01:54.672 --> 00:01:55.505
(gasp)

00:01:55.505 --> 00:01:56.963
- Wait look at the girl on the box.

00:01:56.963 --> 00:01:59.280
- I'm gonna have to say screw the age gap

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:01.183
and just give your four year old

00:02:01.183 --> 00:02:03.871
some balls to throw at his head.

00:02:03.871 --> 00:02:04.804
Should we try it?

00:02:04.804 --> 00:02:05.971
- Lets try it.

00:02:07.739 --> 00:02:09.239
- [Together] Yeay!

00:02:10.963 --> 00:02:13.464
- [Narrator] "My
twenty-something kids loved it."

00:02:13.464 --> 00:02:15.021
- I mean I'd play with
this, I'm twenty-something

00:02:15.021 --> 00:02:16.064
I would play with this.

00:02:16.064 --> 00:02:18.294
- If we could take this out of the box,

00:02:18.294 --> 00:02:21.374
I probably would put it on.

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:22.969
- So yes, definitely review four.

00:02:22.969 --> 00:02:24.991
- I think this would
be a cool gift to like,

00:02:24.991 --> 00:02:29.158
oh congrats on your new
apartment, here's a banana slicer.

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:31.633
- [Narrator] Review five.

00:02:31.633 --> 00:02:33.852
"I use this with my cat
Dwight once a week...

00:02:33.852 --> 00:02:35.196
"It's a win for both of us."

00:02:35.196 --> 00:02:38.344
- I don't think it's the obvious cat book.

00:02:38.344 --> 00:02:39.247
- I don't have a cat.

00:02:39.247 --> 00:02:40.360
- Me either, I had a dog.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:43.173
- It's gotta be crafting
with your cat hair.

00:02:43.173 --> 00:02:46.953
- I think maybe the
twenty-something kids like this,

00:02:46.953 --> 00:02:49.453
and Dwight the cat likes this.

00:02:51.611 --> 00:02:52.948
- [Narrator] "I purchased
this because I was tired

00:02:52.948 --> 00:02:55.755
"Of people sitting too near
me on public transport."

00:02:55.755 --> 00:02:58.321
- Which makes sense for coconut
oil, out of all these things

00:02:58.321 --> 00:03:00.696
because you would just smoosh coconut oil

00:03:00.696 --> 00:03:01.876
on the seat right next to you

00:03:01.876 --> 00:03:03.355
and people will slide right off,

00:03:03.355 --> 00:03:04.424
or they'll look at the seat and be like

00:03:04.424 --> 00:03:07.404
"Ew, it's wet" and they won't sit on it.

00:03:07.404 --> 00:03:08.859
- The cat book.

00:03:08.859 --> 00:03:09.924
- But why?

00:03:09.924 --> 00:03:13.478
- Because people are
freaked out by cat owners.

00:03:13.478 --> 00:03:15.565
- [Narrator] "I posted this
with my (ex) wife's account.

00:03:15.565 --> 00:03:17.265
"She hasn't changed the password yet.

00:03:17.265 --> 00:03:20.030
"We bought this a month ago,
and loved every moment of it.

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:20.863
"She still does.

00:03:20.863 --> 00:03:21.898
"When we went through the divorce,

00:03:21.898 --> 00:03:23.850
"she kept it and left me the kids."

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:25.624
- Oh is it the pickle cause like.

00:03:25.624 --> 00:03:26.666
- I think it's the pickle.

00:03:26.666 --> 00:03:28.248
- We already gave Weird Al that.

00:03:28.248 --> 00:03:30.116
- Maybe Weird Al is the banana slicer.

00:03:30.116 --> 00:03:32.698
- I think it sounds like
some idiot on Amazon,

00:03:32.698 --> 00:03:34.298
who actually doesn't have a wife,

00:03:34.298 --> 00:03:37.525
who thinks that this is
what his wife would like.

00:03:37.525 --> 00:03:41.389
- It's just like so weird,
and it's so specific,

00:03:41.389 --> 00:03:43.808
like an item, you wouldn't be like

00:03:43.808 --> 00:03:47.759
"Oh leave me that little
vacuum cleaner or the kids",

00:03:47.759 --> 00:03:48.697
like it'd be like,

00:03:48.697 --> 00:03:51.008
"leave me that weird
pickle thing or the kids".

00:03:51.008 --> 00:03:53.839
- And they went through a divorce...

00:03:53.839 --> 00:03:55.591
she might need some lovin'.

00:03:55.591 --> 00:03:57.171
- Right.

00:03:57.171 --> 00:04:00.254
(lighthearted music)

00:04:23.271 --> 00:04:24.601
- [Together] What?

00:04:24.601 --> 00:04:25.681
- No!

00:04:25.681 --> 00:04:27.001
- Damnit.

00:04:27.001 --> 00:04:29.281
- What did the wife, I don't know, go on.

00:04:29.281 --> 00:04:31.051
- Jayde needs a banana slicer.

00:04:31.051 --> 00:04:32.601
- I would buy this, 100%.

00:04:32.601 --> 00:04:34.151
- I wish it came in a bigger size,

00:04:34.151 --> 00:04:37.631
but like especially if
you have younger kids

00:04:37.631 --> 00:04:38.481
that you're friends with,

00:04:38.481 --> 00:04:40.531
like maybe little
cousins, nieces, nephews.

00:04:40.531 --> 00:04:42.171
Like that would be a winner.

00:04:42.171 --> 00:04:43.921
Or if you're our age.

